#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:709
#, no-wrap
msgid "Semantic Line Breaks"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:711
msgid ""
"[[https://sembr.org/][Semantic Line Breaks (SemBr)]] is a writing convention "
"where line breaks are placed at logical boundaries in sentences, such as "
"after punctuation marks or between phrases.  This makes diffs more "
"meaningful in version control and improves readability without affecting the "
"rendered output."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:717
msgid ""
"The recommended line length is around 80 characters.  I set this as an upper "
"limit in the editor to prevent lines from becoming unnecessarily long."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:722
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(add-hook 'text-mode-hook\n"
"          (lambda ()\n"
"            (auto-fill-mode 1)\n"
"            (setq fill-column 80)))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:728
#, no-wrap
msgid "org-capture"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:730
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(global-set-key (kbd \"C-c c\") 'org-capture)\n"
"(global-set-key (kbd \"C-c l\") 'org-store-link)"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:733
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq org-root \"~/dropbox/org/\")"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:735
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq org-capture-templates\n"
"      `((\"t\" \"Todo\" entry\n"
"         (file+headline ,(concat org-root \"todo.org\") \"Tasks\")\n"
"         \"* TODO %?\\n  %i\\n  %a\")\n"
"        (\"j\" \"Journal\" entry\n"
"         (file+olp+datetree ,(concat org-root \"journal.org\"))\n"
"         \"* %U\\n%?\\n  %i\\n  %a\")\n"
"        (\"f\" \"Fleeting\" entry\n"
"         (file ,(concat org-root \"fleeting.org\"))\n"
"         \"* %?\\n  %U\\n  %i\\n  %a\")))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:747
#, no-wrap
msgid "org-agenda"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:749
#, no-wrap
msgid "(global-set-key (kbd \"C-c a\") 'org-agenda)"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:751
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq org-agenda-files '(\"~/dropbox/org\"))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:754
msgid ""
"A todo captured with =C-c c t= carries no date, so it never surfaces in the "
"daily agenda and I rediscover it only by scrolling through =todo.org=.  The "
"=u= view lists exactly those entries: TODOs with no SCHEDULED, no DEADLINE, "
"and no active timestamp.  It is the queue I work through when I sit down to "
"plan the week."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:762
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq org-agenda-custom-commands\n"
"      '((\"u\" \"Unscheduled tasks\" alltodo \"\"\n"
"         ((org-agenda-overriding-header \"Unscheduled\")\n"
"          (org-agenda-skip-function\n"
"           '(org-agenda-skip-entry-if 'scheduled 'deadline 'timestamp))))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:769
#, no-wrap
msgid "org-super-agenda"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:771
msgid ""
"[[https://github.com/alphapapa/org-super-agenda][org-super-agenda]] puts "
"agenda items under named headers instead of listing them flat."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:775
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(use-package org-super-agenda\n"
"  :ensure t\n"
"  :hook (org-agenda-mode . org-super-agenda-mode))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:780
msgid ""
"=g= asks the same question as =u= from the other side.  Every TODO stays in "
"the view, grouped by whether it carries a date, so the undated pile sits "
"above the planned work instead of replacing it.  =u= tells me what still "
"needs a date.  =g= tells me whether there is room for any of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:787
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(add-to-list 'org-agenda-custom-commands\n"
"             '(\"g\" \"TODOs grouped by schedule\" alltodo \"\"\n"
"               ((org-super-agenda-groups\n"
"                 '((:name \"No date\" :and (:scheduled nil :deadline nil))\n"
"                   (:name \"Deadline\" :deadline t)\n"
"                   (:name \"Scheduled\" :scheduled t))))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:795
#, no-wrap
msgid "org-habit"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:797
msgid ""
"Some of my todos are things I want to keep doing rather than finish once.  "
"=org-habit= draws a consistency graph next to those entries in the agenda, "
"so a repeating task shows whether I actually kept it up instead of only when "
"it is next due.  Marking an entry as a habit is described in "
"[[https://orgmode.org/manual/Tracking-your-habits.html][Tracking your "
"habits]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:804
msgid ""
"Org ships the module but does not load it by default.  I require the feature "
"after Org loads rather than adding it to =org-modules=, because that option "
"is read once while Org starts up and is easy to set too late."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:810
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(with-eval-after-load 'org\n"
"  (require 'org-habit))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:814
#, no-wrap
msgid "org-gcal"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:816
msgid ""
"[[https://github.com/kidd/org-gcal.el][org-gcal]] provides bidirectional "
"sync between Google Calendar and Org files via the native Google Calendar "
"API."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:820
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(use-package org-gcal\n"
"  :ensure t\n"
"  :defer t)"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:825
msgid "Prerequisites for this configuration to function:"
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 1.
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:830
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the personal Cloud Project, the Google Calendar API is enabled\n"
"and =https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar= is added\n"
"to the OAuth consent screen scopes."
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 2.
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:835
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"=~/.authinfo.age= contains entries:\n"
"#+begin_example\n"
"machine org-gcal login client-id password <client-id>\n"
"machine org-gcal login client-secret password <client-secret>\n"
"#+end_example"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:836
msgid ""
"org-gcal registers an =oauth2-auto= provider entry at package load time only "
"when both =org-gcal-client-id= and =org-gcal-client-secret= are already set; "
"otherwise it skips registration and warns.  Since these variables are "
"populated after the package loads, =org-gcal-reload-client-id-secret= must "
"be called explicitly to perform the registration with the populated values."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:844
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(with-eval-after-load 'org-gcal\n"
"  (setq org-gcal-client-id\n"
"        (auth-source-pick-first-password :host \"org-gcal\" :user "
"\"client-id\"))\n"
"  (setq org-gcal-client-secret\n"
"        (auth-source-pick-first-password :host \"org-gcal\" :user "
"\"client-secret\"))\n"
"  (org-gcal-reload-client-id-secret))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:852
msgid ""
"org-gcal supports only one global OAuth client.  To sync calendars from "
"multiple accounts, share the secondary calendars to the authorized account "
"via Google Calendar's sharing UI with \"Make changes to events\" permission."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:858
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(with-eval-after-load 'org-gcal\n"
"  (setq org-gcal-fetch-file-alist\n"
"        `((\"tomoya.otabi@gmail.com\" . ,(concat org-root "
"\"gcal-personal.org\"))\n"
"          (\"tomoya.otabi@attm.co.jp\" . ,(concat org-root "
"\"gcal-work.org\")))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:864
msgid ""
"I have no use for cancelled events, so I let org-gcal drop their headlines "
"without asking."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:868
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(with-eval-after-load 'org-gcal\n"
"  (setq org-gcal-remove-api-cancelled-events t))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:872
msgid ""
"The plstore holding the OAuth tokens is encrypted symmetrically, so pinentry "
"pops several times per sync unless something caches the passphrase.  "
"=plstore-cache-passphrase-for-symmetric-encryption= keeps it in an Emacs "
"variable for the session, but only under loopback pinentry: that is the one "
"mode in which epg runs the passphrase callback plstore installs, instead of "
"leaving the prompt to gpg-agent and receiving the plaintext alone."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:881
msgid ""
"Caching in gpg-agent rather than in Emacs would survive Emacs restarts, "
"which loopback does not.  It also means dropping =no-symkey-cache= from "
"home-manager's =programs.gpg= defaults, loosening the cache policy of every "
"GPG operation on the machine for the sake of one package.  plstore's own "
"recommendation, public-key encryption via =plstore-encrypt-to=, fits even "
"worse: my encryption subkey lives on a smartcard, so a sync would fail "
"whenever the card is not plugged in."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:892
msgid ""
"Loopback keeps the change inside Emacs, and although the mode is global to "
"epg, plstore is the only epg caller left here now that authinfo is decrypted "
"by age.el and magit signs through git's own gpg invocation.  In exchange the "
"passphrase sits in a variable in cleartext for as long as Emacs runs, and "
"the confirmation prompt is gone, so a typo while recreating the plstore "
"silently becomes the new passphrase."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:903
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq epg-pinentry-mode 'loopback)\n"
"(setq plstore-cache-passphrase-for-symmetric-encryption t)"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:909
msgid ""
"[[https://git.natsukium.com/natsukium/org-clickup][org-clickup]] is a "
"personal package that bidirectionally syncs ClickUp tasks with org-mode TODO "
"entries. Work tasks live in ClickUp, but the authoritative planning surface "
"is org-mode (agenda, capture, refile)  so daily triage stays in Emacs "
"instead of switching to a browser tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:914
msgid "The API token must live in =~/.authinfo.age= as:"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in example
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:917
#, no-wrap
msgid "machine api.clickup.com login <workspace-id> password <token>"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:921
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(use-package org-clickup\n"
"  :ensure t\n"
"  :defer t)"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:926
#, no-wrap
msgid "org-roam"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:928
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(use-package org-roam\n"
"  :ensure t\n"
"  :custom\n"
"  (org-roam-directory \"~/dropbox/org-roam\")\n"
"  (org-roam-db-location \"~/.local/share/org-roam.db\")\n"
"  :bind\n"
"  ((\"C-c n l\" . org-roam-buffer-toggle)\n"
"   (\"C-c n f\" . org-roam-node-find)\n"
"   (\"C-c n g\" . org-roam-graph)\n"
"   (\"C-c n i\" . org-roam-node-insert)\n"
"   (\"C-c n c\" . org-roam-capture)\n"
"   (\"C-c n j\" . org-roam-dailies-capture-today))\n"
"  :config\n"
"  (setq org-roam-capture-templates\n"
"        '((\"p\" \"permanent\" plain \"%?\"\n"
