#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1029
#, no-wrap
msgid "Catching up in one keystroke"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1031
msgid ""
"A Fever update asks for a fixed window of article ids past the last one it "
"saw, so a single fetch never brings in more than "
"=elfeed-protocol-fever-maxsize= entries. I read feeds on several machines "
"and follow daily news through them, so whichever machine I open first has "
"usually fallen days behind, with a backlog of hundreds of articles. Catching "
"up used to mean pressing =G= over and over until nothing new arrived, so "
"=my/elfeed-update-until-done= does the repeating for me, chaining fetches "
"until the server returns nothing."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1040
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar my/elfeed-update-max-rounds 20\n"
"  \"Maximum number of fetch rounds `my/elfeed-update-until-done' will "
"run.\")"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1043
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar my/elfeed--update-rounds (make-hash-table :test #'equal)\n"
"  \"Remaining rounds per protocol feed url while a catch-up run is in "
"flight.\")"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1046
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun my/elfeed-update-until-done ()\n"
"  \"Fetch every protocol feed repeatedly until the server has nothing "
"new.\"\n"
"  (interactive)\n"
"  (dolist (feed-url (elfeed-protocol-feed-list))\n"
"    (my/elfeed--update-round feed-url my/elfeed-update-max-rounds)))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1052
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun my/elfeed--update-round (feed-url rounds)\n"
"  \"Fetch one batch from FEED-URL with ROUNDS fetches left in the "
"budget.\"\n"
"  (let ((update-func (elfeed-protocol-update-func\n"
"                      (elfeed-protocol-type feed-url))))\n"
"    (puthash feed-url rounds my/elfeed--update-rounds)\n"
"    (funcall update-func (elfeed-protocol-url feed-url)\n"
"             (lambda (entries)\n"
"               (my/elfeed--update-continue feed-url entries)))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1061
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun my/elfeed--update-continue (feed-url entries)\n"
"  \"Decide whether to fetch FEED-URL again after a round returned "
"ENTRIES.\"\n"
"  ;; The initial sync splits its request into several batches and runs the\n"
"  ;; callback once per batch.  Clearing the budget before deciding makes "
"the\n"
"  ;; later callbacks no-ops instead of forking the chain.\n"
"  (when-let* ((rounds (gethash feed-url my/elfeed--update-rounds)))\n"
"    (remhash feed-url my/elfeed--update-rounds)\n"
"    ;; Each feed's chain ends asynchronously in one of the first two "
"branches,\n"
"    ;; so there is no single \"all feeds done\" point where expiry could "
"run\n"
"    ;; once.  Running it per finished chain is redundant but idempotent.\n"
"    (cond\n"
"     ((null entries)\n"
"      (message \"elfeed: %s is up to date\" feed-url)\n"
"      (my/elfeed-expire-entries))\n"
"     ((<= rounds 1)\n"
"      (message \"elfeed: %s still had entries after %d rounds\"\n"
"               feed-url my/elfeed-update-max-rounds)\n"
"      (my/elfeed-expire-entries))\n"
"     (t\n"
"      (message \"elfeed: fetched %d entries from %s\" (length entries) "
"feed-url)\n"
"      ;; The pause is not politeness toward Miniflux; it moves the next\n"
"      ;; request out of the curl process filter that delivered this "
"response.\n"
"      (run-at-time 1 nil #'my/elfeed--update-round feed-url (1- rounds))))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1085
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(with-eval-after-load 'elfeed-search\n"
"  (keymap-set elfeed-search-mode-map \"G\" #'my/elfeed-update-until-done))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1089
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gaps in Fever article ids"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1091
msgid ""
"That fixed window poses a sharper problem than merely slowing down "
"catch-up.  The window is a literal list of ids rather than a request for "
"everything newer, and Miniflux deletes old entries, so the ids on the server "
"are not contiguous. A machine that has been away long enough for every id in "
"its window to have been deleted gets an empty answer, never advances its "
"stored last id, and stops receiving articles for good. Nothing is logged, "
"because an empty result looks exactly like being up to date, and the "
"catch-up loop above cannot help either: every round recomputes the same dead "
"window."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1100
msgid ""
"One of my machines fell six months behind and landed in front of a run of "
"318 deleted ids, far beyond the reach of the default 50-id window. A 500-id "
"window crosses a gap of that size in one fetch. That is a wider margin "
"rather than a permanent fix. A longer run of deleted ids would strand a "
"machine again, and recovering from it requires manually setting the mark "
"past the gap with =elfeed-protocol-fever-set-update-mark=."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1108
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq elfeed-protocol-fever-maxsize 500)"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1111
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expiring news"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1113
msgid ""
"News articles arrive in volume and are worth reading the week they appear "
"and never again, so keeping them around only bloats the local "
"database. Entries tagged =news= are deleted once they are older than a "
"month, at the end of every catch-up run."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar my/elfeed-expire-tag 'news\n"
"  \"Tag whose entries `my/elfeed-expire-entries' retires.\")"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defvar my/elfeed-expire-age \"1 month\"\n"
"  \"Age past which entries tagged `my/elfeed-expire-tag' are removed.\")"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun my/elfeed-expire-entries ()\n"
"  \"Remove aged out entries tagged `my/elfeed-expire-tag' from the "
"database.\"\n"
"  (interactive)\n"
"  (let ((threshold (- (float-time) (elfeed-time-duration "
"my/elfeed-expire-age)))\n"
"        (expired ()))\n"
"    ;; Collect before deleting; `elfeed-db-visit' walks the same tree the\n"
"    ;; deletion mutates.\n"
"    (with-elfeed-db-visit (entry)\n"
"      (when (and (elfeed-tagged-p my/elfeed-expire-tag entry)\n"
"                 (< (elfeed-entry-date entry) threshold))\n"
"        (push entry expired)))\n"
"    (when expired\n"
"      ;; Untag before deleting so elfeed-protocol pushes the read state to\n"
"      ;; Miniflux; an entry deleted while still unread would leave the "
"server\n"
"      ;; counting an article that no longer exists locally.\n"
"      (elfeed-untag expired 'unread)\n"
"      (elfeed-db-delete expired)\n"
"      (when (get-buffer \"*elfeed-search*\")\n"
"        (elfeed-search-update :force))\n"
"      (message \"elfeed: expired %d %s entries\"\n"
"               (length expired) my/elfeed-expire-tag))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading *
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1148
#, no-wrap
msgid "mail"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1150
msgid ""
"[[https://notmuchmail.org/][notmuch]] is a tag-based email indexer and "
"searcher.  [[https://notmuchmail.org/notmuch-emacs/][notmuch.el]] provides "
"an Emacs interface for reading and organizing email.  It reads mail from a "
"local maildir synced by mbsync."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1154
msgid ""
"notmuch was chosen over mu4e because the notmuch indexer is already "
"configured for all email accounts.  Adding notmuch.el only requires the "
"Emacs frontend, avoiding a second indexer for the same maildir."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1159
msgid ""
"notmuch has no built-in delete operation; it manages metadata (tags)  rather "
"than maildir folder placement.  Pressing =d= tags the message with "
"=+deleted= and removes =inbox=.  The actual deletion happens on the next "
"=notmuch new=: a post-new hook moves tagged files to Gmail's Trash maildir "
"folder after indexing, so the move is synced to the server on the next "
"mbsync run.  =D= reverses the operation, restoring =inbox= and removing "
"=deleted=.  This only works before the next =notmuch new= moves the file; "
"once mbsync has synced the move, the message is in Gmail's Trash."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1169
msgid ""
"=shr-use-colors= is disabled so sender HTML colors don't clash with the dark "
"theme. Inline CID images ship with the mail and are enabled, but "
"=shr-blocked-images= is set to =.= (matches every URL) to block remote "
"images, which marketing platforms use as tracking pixels — Gmail's web UI "
"proxies them, but notmuch fetches directly. =I= refreshes the current "
"message with blocking disabled when a sender is trusted."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1176
msgid ""
"=notmuch-show-part-button-default-action= defaults to saving an attachment "
"to disk; I switch it to =notmuch-show-view-part= so the part opens with its "
"mailcap viewer instead, letting me press the button on a PDF to open it "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(use-package notmuch\n"
"  :ensure nil\n"
"  :bind (\"C-c M\" . notmuch)\n"
"  :custom\n"
"  (notmuch-fcc-dirs nil)\n"
"  (notmuch-search-oldest-first nil)\n"
"  (notmuch-show-part-button-default-action 'notmuch-show-view-part)\n"
"  (notmuch-saved-searches\n"
"   '((:name \"inbox\"    :query \"tag:inbox\"                                      "
":key \"i\")\n"
"     (:name \"unread\"   :query \"tag:unread\"                                     "
":key \"u\")\n"
"     (:name \"action\"   :query \"tag:github::action-required\"                    "
":key \"a\")\n"
"     (:name \"attmcojp\" :query \"tag:github::attmcojp\"                           "
":key \"w\")\n"
"     (:name \"github\"   :query \"tag:github and not "
"tag:github::action-required\" :key \"g\")\n"
"     (:name \"all\"      :query \"*\"                                              "
":key \"A\")))\n"
"  (shr-use-colors nil)\n"
"  (mm-inline-text-html-with-images t)\n"
"  (shr-blocked-images \".\")\n"
"  :config\n"
"  (keymap-set notmuch-search-mode-map \"d\"\n"
"    (lambda ()\n"
"      (interactive)\n"
"      (notmuch-search-tag '(\"+deleted\" \"-inbox\"))\n"
"      (notmuch-search-next-thread)))\n"
"  (keymap-set notmuch-show-mode-map \"d\"\n"
"    (lambda ()\n"
"      (interactive)\n"
"      (notmuch-show-tag '(\"+deleted\" \"-inbox\"))))\n"
"  (keymap-set notmuch-search-mode-map \"D\"\n"
"    (lambda ()\n"
"      (interactive)\n"
"      (notmuch-search-tag '(\"-deleted\" \"+inbox\"))\n"
"      (notmuch-search-next-thread)))\n"
"  (keymap-set notmuch-show-mode-map \"D\"\n"
"    (lambda ()\n"
"      (interactive)\n"
"      (notmuch-show-tag '(\"-deleted\" \"+inbox\"))))\n"
"  (keymap-set notmuch-show-mode-map \"I\"\n"
"    (lambda ()\n"
"      (interactive)\n"
"      (let ((shr-blocked-images nil))\n"
"        (notmuch-show-refresh-view t)))))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1225
msgid ""
"[[https://orgmode.org/manual/Protocols.html][ol-notmuch]] integrates notmuch "
"with Org mode's link system.  Calling =org-store-link= (=C-c l=) in a "
"notmuch buffer stores a link to the current message or thread, which can "
"then be inserted into org-capture templates via =%a=."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/features/editor/emacs/init.org:1231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(use-package ol-notmuch\n"
"  :ensure t\n"
"  :after (notmuch org))"
msgstr ""

