#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1478
#, no-wrap
msgid "System Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1480
msgid ""
"macOS builds the system =PATH= with =path_helper=, which Apple's shell "
"profiles run at login. It reads =/etc/paths= and =/etc/paths.d=, puts those "
"directories first, and appends whatever =PATH= it inherited. Under nix that "
"ordering is backwards: =/usr/bin= lands ahead of the nix profiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1485
msgid ""
"nix-darwin and nixpkgs already avoid it. The =/etc/zprofile= nix-darwin "
"installs over Apple's has no =path_helper= call, and nixpkgs patches fish to "
"skip =path_helper= when =__NIX_DARWIN_SET_ENVIRONMENT_DONE= is set, the flag "
"nix-darwin exports once it has built =PATH= itself. Apple's =/etc/profile= "
"is the one file neither of them owns. Nothing repairs the damage afterwards "
"either, because the =/etc/bashrc= that =/etc/profile= goes on to source only "
"runs =set-environment= while that same flag is unset. A login =sh= therefore "
"ends up with =/usr/bin= first, and finds the Xcode command line tools stub "
"instead of my =git=."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1494
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-etc-profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1496
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"environment.etc.\"profile\" = {\n"
"  knownSha256Hashes = [ "
"\"a3fe9f414586c0d3cacbe3b6920a09d8718e503bca22e23fef882203bf765065\" ];\n"
"  text = ''"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1503
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    if [ \"''${BASH-no}\" != \"no\" ]; then\n"
"      [ -r /etc/bashrc ] && . /etc/bashrc\n"
"    fi\n"
"  '';\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1510
#, no-wrap
msgid "History"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1512
msgid ""
"History is stored under =XDG_CONFIG_HOME= to keep =$HOME= clean, consistent "
"with the repository's preference for XDG base directories (see [[*User-Level "
"Settings][User-Level Settings]])."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1515
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-history"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1517
#, no-wrap
msgid "historyFile = \"$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bash/history\";"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1520
#, no-wrap
msgid "Completion"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1522
msgid ""
"Bash completion is disabled because bash is not used as the primary "
"interactive shell. Loading completion scripts adds startup time (~100ms+) "
"with no benefit when the shell is only used as a fallback or for running "
"scripts."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1526
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-completion"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1528
#, no-wrap
msgid "enableCompletion = false;"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1531
#, no-wrap
msgid "Aliases"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1533
msgid ""
"Basic aliases that provide a minimal quality-of-life improvement if bash is "
"used interactively. These are intentionally simple — fish handles the rich "
"interactive experience."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1537
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-aliases"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1539
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"shellAliases = {\n"
"  l = \"ls -CF\";\n"
"  grep = \"grep --color=auto\";\n"
"  fgrep = \"fgrep --color=auto\";\n"
"  egrep = \"egrep --color=auto\";\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1547
#, no-wrap
msgid "Init"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1549
msgid ""
"This configuration is a remnant from before fish was set as the default "
"login shell.  Previously, bash was the login shell and =.bashrc= launched "
"fish, so these settings were needed in every interactive session. They are "
"retained because bash is still used as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1554
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-init"
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list +
#: modules/configuration.org:1561
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"lib.optionalString (!config.programs.kitty.enable) ''\n"
"<<bash-tmux-autostart>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1556
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"initExtra = ''\n"
"  <<bash-terminal-settings>>\n"
"''\n"
"'';"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:1564
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terminal Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1566
msgid ""
"=stty stop undef= disables =Ctrl+S= from sending =XOFF=, freeing it for use "
"as a keybinding in fish and other TUI applications. Without it, =Ctrl+S= "
"freezes the terminal until =Ctrl+Q= is pressed."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1570
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-terminal-settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1572
#, no-wrap
msgid "stty stop undef  # Ctrl-s"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:1575
#, no-wrap
msgid "TMUX Auto-attach"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1577
msgid ""
"Automatically starts or attaches to a tmux session when bash is the "
"interactive shell, but only when kitty is not the terminal emulator. Kitty "
"has its own tab/window management (splits, layouts, tabs) that conflicts "
"with tmux's multiplexing — running tmux inside kitty creates redundant "
"nesting. When using a simpler terminal (e.g., =xterm=, =alacritty=, or a "
"Linux console), tmux provides the session persistence and window management "
"that would otherwise be missing."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1584
#, no-wrap
msgid "bash-tmux-autostart"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1587
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"if type tmux > /dev/null 2>&1; then\n"
"  test -z $TMUX && tmux"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1592
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  while test -z $TMUX; do\n"
"    tmux attach || break\n"
"  done\n"
"fi"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/configuration.org:1598
#, no-wrap
msgid "Readline"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1600
msgid ""
"readline provides line editing for bash and for most REPLs with a plain "
"prompt, such as the Python interpreter and =psql=. Configuring it here "
"rather than through bash keybindings covers all of them at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1604
msgid ""
"=Ctrl+W= deletes back to the previous =/= rather than the previous word "
"boundary, which suits the paths that make up most of what I type at a "
"prompt. The binding only holds with =bind-tty-special-chars= off: readline "
"otherwise copies the terminal's =werase= character into its keymap after "
"reading =inputrc=, which puts =Ctrl+W= back on =unix-word-rubout=."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1610
msgid "=completion-ignore-case= makes tab completion case-insensitive."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1618
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{ ... }:\n"
"{\n"
"  flake.modules.homeManager.readline =\n"
"    {\n"
"      lib,\n"
"      config,\n"
"      ...\n"
"    }:\n"
"    let\n"
"      cfg = config.my.programs.readline;\n"
"    in\n"
"    {\n"
"      options.my.programs.readline.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"readline\";"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1632
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"config = lib.mkIf cfg.enable {\n"
"  programs.readline = {\n"
"    enable = true;"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1636
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"variables = {\n"
"  completion-ignore-case = true;\n"
"  bind-tty-special-chars = false;\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1641
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"          bindings = {\n"
"            \"\\\\C-w\" = \"unix-filename-rubout\";\n"
"          };\n"
"        };\n"
"      };\n"
"    };\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/configuration.org:1650
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nushell"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1652
msgid ""
"Nushell is enabled for its ability to handle structured data natively, "
"similar to PowerShell. Where traditional shells pipe text between commands, "
"Nushell operates on serialised data formats (JSON, YAML, CSV, etc.) as "
"first-class tables and records, making simple data manipulation possible "
"without reaching for external tools like =jq=.  Like fish, it is non-POSIX, "
"but POSIX compatibility is not a requirement for an interactive shell."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1659
msgid ""
"No custom configuration is added yet — the defaults are sufficient for "
"exploratory use, and committing to Nushell-specific workflows would be "
"premature."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1662
msgid ""
"Registered behind =my.programs.nushell.enable=, like the other shells in "
"this section."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1670
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{ ... }:\n"
"{\n"
"  flake.modules.homeManager.nushell =\n"
"    {\n"
"      config,\n"
"      lib,\n"
"      pkgs,\n"
"      ...\n"
"    }:\n"
"    let\n"
"      cfg = config.my.programs.nushell;\n"
"      completerCfg = config.ext.programs.nushell.externalCompleter;\n"
"    in\n"
"    {\n"
"      options.my.programs.nushell.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"nushell\";"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1686
#, no-wrap
msgid "<<nushell-external-completer-option>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1688
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"config = lib.mkMerge [\n"
"  (lib.mkIf cfg.enable {\n"
"    programs.nushell.enable = true;\n"
"  })"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1693
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <<nushell-external-completer-config>>\n"
"      ];\n"
"    };\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1699
#, no-wrap
msgid "External Completer"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1701
msgid ""
"Nushell has no built-in tab-completion source for external (non-Nushell)  "
"commands. Piping candidates through fish's own completion engine reuses "
"every completion already defined for fish — package names, git subcommands, "
"CLI flags — instead of duplicating that logic in Nushell's completer syntax."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1706
msgid ""
"=externalCompleter= defaults to following whether Nushell itself is enabled, "
"so enabling the shell is enough to get external completions without a second "
"toggle; =enableFishCompleter= exists to opt out if fish is not the shell "
"doing the completing."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1711
#, no-wrap
msgid "nushell-external-completer-option"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1713
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"options.ext.programs.nushell.externalCompleter = {\n"
"  enable = lib.mkOption {\n"
"    type = lib.types.bool;\n"
"    default = config.programs.nushell.enable;\n"
"  };\n"
"  enableFishCompleter = lib.mkOption {\n"
"    type = lib.types.bool;\n"
"    default = true;\n"
"  };\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1725
#, no-wrap
msgid "nushell-external-completer-config"
msgstr ""

#. type: cell column 0
#: modules/configuration.org:1731
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\"value(char tab)description(char newline)\" + $in"
msgstr ""

#. type: cell column 0
#: modules/configuration.org:1732
#, no-wrap
msgid "from tsv --flexible --no-infer"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1727
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(lib.mkIf completerCfg.enable {\n"
"  programs.nushell.extraConfig = lib.mkIf completerCfg.enableFishCompleter "
"''\n"
"    let fish_completer = {|spans|\n"
"        ${lib.getExe pkgs.fish} --command $'complete \"--do-complete=($spans "
"| str join \" \")\"'\n"
"    }"
msgstr ""

#. type: cell column 0
#: modules/configuration.org:1739
#, no-wrap
msgid "default {}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cell column 0
#: modules/configuration.org:1740
#, no-wrap
msgid "insert enable { true }"
msgstr ""

#. type: cell column 0
#: modules/configuration.org:1741
#, no-wrap
msgid "insert completer { $fish_completer }"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1735
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    $env.config = ($env.config? | default {})\n"
"    $env.config.completions = ($env.config.completions? | default {})\n"
"    $env.config.completions.external = (\n"
"        $env.config.completions.external?\n"
"    )\n"
"  '';\n"
"})"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/configuration.org:1747
#, no-wrap
msgid "Starship"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1749
msgid ""
"[[https://starship.rs/][Starship]] is a cross-shell prompt written in Rust, "
"used across all shells configured here to provide a consistent prompt "
"experience. It has been used since its predecessor "
"[[https://github.com/matchai/spacefish][spacefish]], and its easy TOML-based "
"configuration is the main reason it has been kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1753
msgid ""
"Starship does not natively support asynchronous prompt rendering, so this "
"section also includes a custom async prompt module for fish."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1756
msgid ""
"Registered behind =my.programs.starship.enable=, with "
"=enableFishAsyncPrompt= as a second, independent toggle on the same module — "
"a host can run starship without the async prompt, but not the reverse."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1766
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{ ... }:\n"
"{\n"
"  flake.modules.homeManager.starship =\n"
"    {\n"
"      config,\n"
"      lib,\n"
"      ...\n"
"    }:\n"
"    let\n"
"      cfg = config.my.programs.starship;\n"
"    in\n"
"    {\n"
"      options.my.programs.starship = {\n"
"        enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"starship\";"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1781
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  enableFishAsyncPrompt = lib.mkOption {\n"
"    type = lib.types.bool;\n"
"    default = false;\n"
"  };\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1787
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"config = lib.mkMerge [\n"
"  (lib.mkIf cfg.enable {\n"
"    programs.starship = {\n"
"      enable = true;\n"
"      settings = builtins.fromTOML (builtins.readFile ./starship.toml);\n"
"    };\n"
"  })"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1795
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <<starship-async-prompt-config>>\n"
"      ];\n"
"    };\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1806
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prompt Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1808
msgid ""
"The prompt format prepends a shell indicator before the default modules.  "
"This makes it immediately visible which shell is active, useful when "
"switching between fish and bash for testing or debugging."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1813
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"$schema\" = \"https://starship.rs/config-schema.json\""
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1815
#, no-wrap
msgid "format = \"$shell$all$line_break$character\""
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1818
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell Indicator"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1820
msgid ""
"Each shell has a distinct icon: =󰈺= (fish icon) for fish. Bash and nushell "
"use the default indicator."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1824
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[shell]\n"
"fish_indicator = \"󰈺\"\n"
"powershell_indicator = \"󰨊\"\n"
"disabled = false"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1830
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remote Container Detection"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1832
msgid ""
"A custom module detects when running inside a VS Code Remote Container (Dev "
"Container) by checking the =REMOTE_CONTAINERS= environment variable, "
"displaying a whale emoji (🐋) as a visual reminder. This has not been used "
"for several years and may no longer be relevant."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1838
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[custom.remote-container]\n"
"when = \"\"\" test \"$REMOTE_CONTAINERS\" \"\"\"\n"
"symbol = \"🐋\"\n"
"format = \" in $symbol \""
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1844
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disabled Modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1846
msgid ""
"=gcloud= is disabled because it reads the active GCP configuration from the "
"home directory (=~/.config/gcloud/=), causing it to appear in every "
"repository regardless of whether the project uses GCP."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1851
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[gcloud]\n"
"disabled = true"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:1855
#, no-wrap
msgid "Async Prompt Module"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1857
msgid ""
"Starship's default fish integration is replaced with an asynchronous "
"variant, gated on the same module's =enableFishAsyncPrompt= toggle rather "
"than a separate file, since the two options always travel together. The "
"async prompt script is cherry-picked from "
"[[https://gist.github.com/duament/bac0181935953b97ca71640727c9c029][duament's "
"gist]], based on "
"[[https://github.com/acomagu/fish-async-prompt][fish-async-prompt]].  See "
"also "
"[[https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/issues/8223][fish-shell#8223]] "
"for upstream discussion on async prompt support."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:1864
#, no-wrap
msgid "starship-async-prompt-config"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1866
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(lib.mkIf cfg.enableFishAsyncPrompt {\n"
"  programs.starship.enableFishIntegration = lib.mkForce false;"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1870
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  programs.fish.interactiveShellInit = ''\n"
"    if test \"$TERM\" != dumb\n"
"        ${lib.getExe config.programs.starship.package} init fish | source\n"
"        source ${./async_prompt.fish}\n"
"    end\n"
"  '';\n"
"})"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:1879
#, no-wrap
msgid "Async Prompt Script"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1888
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"status is-interactive\n"
"or exit 0"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1891
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"if test -n \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"\n"
"    set -g __starship_async_tmpdir \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"/fish-async-prompt\n"
"else\n"
"    set -g __starship_async_tmpdir /tmp/fish-async-prompt\n"
"end\n"
"mkdir -p \"$__starship_async_tmpdir\"\n"
"set -g __starship_async_signal SIGUSR1"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1900
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"set -g VIRTUAL_ENV_DISABLE_PROMPT 1\n"
"builtin functions -e fish_mode_prompt\n"
"set -gx STARSHIP_SHELL fish\n"
"set -gx STARSHIP_SESSION_KEY (random 10000000000000 9999999999999999)"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1906
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function fish_prompt\n"
"    printf '\\e[0J' # Clear from cursor to end of screen\n"
"    if test -e \"$__starship_async_tmpdir\"/\"$fish_pid\"_fish_prompt\n"
"        cat \"$__starship_async_tmpdir\"/\"$fish_pid\"_fish_prompt\n"
"    else\n"
"        __starship_async_simple_prompt\n"
"    end\n"
"end"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1916
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function __starship_async_fire --on-event fish_prompt\n"
"    switch \"$fish_key_bindings\"\n"
"        case fish_hybrid_key_bindings fish_vi_key_bindings\n"
"            set STARSHIP_KEYMAP \"$fish_bind_mode\"\n"
"        case '*'\n"
"            set STARSHIP_KEYMAP insert\n"
"    end\n"
"    set STARSHIP_CMD_PIPESTATUS $pipestatus\n"
"    set STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS $status\n"
"    set STARSHIP_DURATION \"$CMD_DURATION\"\n"
"    set STARSHIP_JOBS (count (jobs -p))"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1928
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    set -l tmpfile \"$__starship_async_tmpdir\"/\"$fish_pid\"_fish_prompt\n"
"    fish -c '\n"
"starship prompt --terminal-width=\"'$COLUMNS'\" "
"--status='$STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS' --pipestatus=\"'$STARSHIP_CMD_PIPESTATUS'\" "
"--keymap='$STARSHIP_KEYMAP' --cmd-duration='$STARSHIP_DURATION' "
"--jobs='$STARSHIP_JOBS' > '$tmpfile'\n"
"kill -s \"'$__starship_async_signal'\" '$fish_pid &\n"
"    disown\n"
"end"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1935
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function __starship_async_simple_prompt\n"
"    set_color brgreen\n"
"    echo -n '❯'\n"
"    set_color normal\n"
"    echo ' '\n"
"end"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1942
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function __starship_async_repaint_prompt --on-signal "
"\"$__starship_async_signal\"\n"
"    commandline -f repaint\n"
"end"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1946
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function __starship_async_cleanup --on-event fish_exit\n"
"    rm -f \"$__starship_async_tmpdir\"/\"$fish_pid\"_fish_prompt\n"
"end"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading *
#: modules/configuration.org:1954
#, no-wrap
msgid "Version Control"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/configuration.org:1956
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1958
msgid ""
"Git version control configuration. Git is configured directly through "
"home-manager's =programs.git= module, which generates =~/.config/git/config= "
"declaratively."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:1961
msgid ""
"Registered behind =my.programs.git.enable=. The [[*Scalar][Scalar]] "
"performance tuning below is a second, independent toggle on the same module "
"rather than a separate file, since scalar has no meaning without the git "
"module it extends."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1971
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{ ... }:\n"
"{\n"
"  flake.modules.homeManager.git =\n"
"    {\n"
"      config,\n"
"      lib,\n"
"      ...\n"
"    }:\n"
"    let\n"
"      cfg = config.my.programs.git;\n"
"      scalarCfg = config.programs.git.scalar;\n"
"    in\n"
"    {\n"
"      options.my.programs.git.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"git\";"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1986
#, no-wrap
msgid "<<git-scalar-option>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:1988
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
