#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:2872
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSH Port"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:2874
msgid ""
"Tailscale runs with [[*Service Settings][=--ssh=]], so on the tailnet "
"tailscaled answers port 22 itself and hands out a plain shell as "
"=forgejo=. That bypasses the ~command=\"forgejo serv\"~ restriction git "
"depends on, so sshd moves to 2022.  =SSH_PORT= is pinned to 22 anyway: "
"forgejo only uses it to render clone URLs, and any other value turns them "
"into full ~ssh://~ URIs. The [[*SSH Route][ssh route]] on the client carries "
"the real port."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:2881
#, no-wrap
msgid "forgejo-ssh-port"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2883
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"services.openssh.ports = [ 2022 ];\n"
"services.forgejo.settings.server.SSH_PORT = 22;"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:2887
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instance Signing"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:2889
msgid ""
"Forgejo authors the commit itself when I merge a pull request or edit a file "
"in the web UI, so those commits carry no signature. An instance key signs "
"them, in the same SSH format as [[*Commit Signing][my own commits]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:2893
#, no-wrap
msgid "forgejo-signing"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2895
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sops.secrets.forgejo-signing-key = {\n"
"  sopsFile = ./secrets.yaml;\n"
"  owner = \"forgejo\";\n"
"  path = \"/var/lib/forgejo-signing/key\";\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2901
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"systemd.tmpfiles.settings.\"10-forgejo-signing\" = {\n"
"  \"/var/lib/forgejo-signing\".d = {\n"
"    user = \"forgejo\";\n"
"    group = \"forgejo\";\n"
"    mode = \"0750\";\n"
"  };\n"
"  \"${config.sops.secrets.forgejo-signing-key.path}.pub\".\"L+\".argument = "
"toString (\n"
"    pkgs.writeText \"forgejo-signing-key.pub\" \"ssh-ed25519 "
"AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAWHoqNuRjeO1o4x6pdrF3ZCZRluh80HWVP6X8j4k8pn "
"forgejo@natsukium.com\\n\"\n"
"  );\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2912
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"services.forgejo.settings.\"repository.signing\" = {\n"
"  FORMAT = \"ssh\";\n"
"  SIGNING_KEY = \"${config.sops.secrets.forgejo-signing-key.path}.pub\";\n"
"  SIGNING_NAME = \"Forgejo\";\n"
"  SIGNING_EMAIL = \"forgejo@natsukium.com\";\n"
"  MERGES = \"always\";\n"
"  CRUD_ACTIONS = \"always\";\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2921
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemd.services.forgejo.path = [ pkgs.openssh ];"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:2924
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backup"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:2926
msgid ""
"The repositories under =stateDir= are only half the instance: issues, users "
"and access tokens live in postgres, and restoring one without the other "
"leaves a Forgejo that cannot serve any of it. Upstream's =forgejo dump= is "
"not an alternative: it warns that its own SQL dump has long-standing "
"re-import bugs, and its zip would arrive as a fresh opaque blob every time, "
"leaving restic nothing to deduplicate against yesterday's."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:2933
#, no-wrap
msgid "forgejo-backup"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2935
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"services.postgresqlBackup = {\n"
"  enable = true;\n"
"  databases = [ config.services.forgejo.database.name ];\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2940
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"my.services.restic.backups.forgejo.paths = [\n"
"  config.services.forgejo.stateDir\n"
"  "
"\"${config.services.postgresqlBackup.location}/${config.services.forgejo.database.name}.sql.gz\"\n"
"];"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ***
#: modules/configuration.org:2946
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:2948
msgid ""
"What every machine of mine needs to talk to the instance: where ssh goes, "
"and which remotes take that route."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:2951
#, no-wrap
msgid "forgejo-client"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2953
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flake.modules.homeManager.forgejo =\n"
"  { config, lib, ... }:\n"
"  {\n"
"    options.my.programs.forgejo.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"the ssh route "
"to my forge\";"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2958
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"config = lib.mkIf config.my.programs.forgejo.enable {\n"
"  <<forgejo-ssh-route>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2961
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <<forgejo-push-url>>\n"
"  };\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:2966
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSH Route"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:2968
msgid ""
"=git.natsukium.com= resolves publicly to the cloudflared tunnel, which "
"carries HTTP only, so ssh needs another path. Every machine of mine reaches "
"manyara over tailscale, so this block points the public name at the tailnet "
"one. It lands in =~/.ssh/config= through the [[*SSH Client][SSH Client]] "
"module, which owns the file."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:2973
#, no-wrap
msgid "forgejo-ssh-route"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2975
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"programs.ssh.settings.\"git.natsukium.com\" = {\n"
"  HostName = \"manyara.tail4108.ts.net\";\n"
"  Port = 2022;\n"
"};"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading ****
#: modules/configuration.org:2981
#, no-wrap
msgid "Push URLs"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:2983
msgid ""
"Remotes cloned over https would push over https as well. This rewrite routes "
"every push to the forge over ssh instead, leaving fetch on the tunnel."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:2986
#, no-wrap
msgid "forgejo-push-url"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:2988
#, no-wrap
