#. type: heading *
#: modules/configuration.org:4989
#, no-wrap
msgid "Browser"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:4991
msgid ""
"Compared with Chromium, Firefox lets me declare far more of its "
"configuration (search engines and extensions, to name two), and that plays "
"straight into home-manager: every machine gets the same browser from the "
"same expression, with no sync service involved. That is why I stay on the "
"Firefox side of the fence. I also simply want to run Gecko rather than yet "
"another Blink browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:4997
msgid ""
"For about a year and a half that Firefox was [[https://zen-browser.app/][Zen "
"Browser]], a fork with better UI/UX, though I always had some reservations "
"about it. While I was using it, stock Firefox kept shipping, and eventually "
"almost everything I wanted landed upstream:"
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 1.
#: modules/configuration.org:5004
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Vertical tabs "
"([[https://www.firefox.com/en-US/firefox/136.0/releasenotes/][Firefox "
"136]]). I keep a hundred tabs open at all times, so a\n"
"horizontal tab strip is out of the question."
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 2.
#: modules/configuration.org:5006
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Configurable keyboard shortcuts "
"([[https://www.firefox.com/en-US/firefox/147.0/releasenotes/][Firefox "
"147]]). Firefox finally lets me rebind\n"
"them."
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 3.
#: modules/configuration.org:5008
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Split view "
"([[https://www.firefox.com/en-US/firefox/149.0/releasenotes/][Firefox "
"149]]). Not an everyday feature, but comparing two pages\n"
"side by side comes up more often than I expected."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5009
msgid "What I liked about Zen beyond that turned out to need nothing more than CSS:"
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 1.
#: modules/configuration.org:5013
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[[https://docs.zen-browser.app/user-manual/compact-mode][Compact mode]]. A "
"browser, like almost every program, has no need for bars;\n"
"Zen hides the toolbar and sidebar by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: plain list 2.
#: modules/configuration.org:5018
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[[https://docs.zen-browser.app/user-manual/urlbar][Floating URL bar]]. Zen's "
"URL bar searches like any other, but the input\n"
"floats in the middle of the window. URL bars are normally pinned to the top "
"or\n"
"bottom edge, so one of the most heavily used components demands the longest "
"eye\n"
"movement. And as compact mode shows, I don't want a bar there in the first\n"
"place."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5019
msgid ""
"Neither needs a fork; a =userChrome.css= theme is enough. With "
"[[https://github.com/reizumii/parfait][parfait]] I get everything I wanted "
"from Zen on stock Firefox, and it is far from the only such theme; "
"[[https://github.com/greeeen-dev/natsumi-browser][natsumi-browser]] was the "
"first one I came across."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5023
msgid ""
"With the UI gap closed, what remains are my reservations: Zen's stability, "
"its prospects as a project, and how well it is maintained in nixpkgs. So I "
"switched to Firefox and removed Zen from the configuration entirely."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:5033
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{ ... }:\n"
"let\n"
"  sharedSearch = import ./search.nix;\n"
"  sharedExtensions = import ./extensions.nix;\n"
"in\n"
"{\n"
"  <<firefox-module>>\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/configuration.org:5043
#, no-wrap
msgid "Firefox"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5045
msgid ""
"Stock Firefox is dressed in parfait, a chrome theme written entirely in "
"=userChrome.css= (no extension, no =userChrome.js= loader), so it lives "
"inside the profile home-manager already writes."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5050
msgid ""
"On Linux, home-manager still defaults the profile directory to "
"=~/.mozilla/firefox= for =home.stateVersion= below 26.05 and warns on every "
"evaluation until the choice is made explicit."
msgstr ""

#. type: keyword NAME
#: modules/configuration.org:5054
#, no-wrap
msgid "firefox-module"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:5056
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"flake.modules.homeManager.firefox =\n"
"  {\n"
"    config,\n"
"    lib,\n"
"    pkgs,\n"
"    ...\n"
"  }:\n"
"  let\n"
"    cfg = config.my.programs.firefox;\n"
"    parfait = pkgs.callPackage ./parfait.nix { };\n"
"    workContainerId = 1;\n"
"  in\n"
"  {\n"
"    options.my.programs.firefox = {\n"
"      enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Firefox\";\n"
"    };"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph in src
#: modules/configuration.org:5073
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"config = lib.mkIf cfg.enable {\n"
"  programs.firefox = {\n"
"    enable = true;\n"
"    configPath = lib.mkIf pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.isLinux "
"\"${config.xdg.configHome}/mozilla/firefox\";\n"
"    profiles.natsukium = {\n"
"      search = sharedSearch { inherit pkgs; };\n"
"      extensions = sharedExtensions { inherit pkgs; } // {\n"
"        <<firefox-containerise-rules>>\n"
"      };"
msgstr ""

