#. type: heading *
#: modules/configuration.org:5835
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terminal"
msgstr ""

#. type: heading **
#: modules/configuration.org:5837
#, no-wrap
msgid "Felis"
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5839
msgid ""
"[[https://git.natsukium.com/natsukium/felis][felis]] is a daemon/client "
"terminal whose defining feature is session persistence across hosts. Apart "
"from the client set up on desktops, deploying the daemon in every "
"environment keeps a session running stably even over SSH."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5843
msgid ""
"The client names a separate "
"[[https://github.com/yuru7/moralerspace][Moralerspace]] flavor per text "
"style — Neon, Xenon, Radon, Krypton. felis derives bold and italic from a "
"family's own faces, but these flavors are separate families rather than "
"weights of one, so naming them per style is the only way to reach them."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5848
msgid ""
"Two keymap entries work around problems outside felis. On a JIS keyboard the "
"yen key still types =¥= though macOS is set to emit =\\=, because winit "
"drops the substituted character unless an IME preedit is active; rebinding "
"it here avoids waiting for a winit release. Shift+Enter already goes out as "
"=CSI 13;2u= under the Kitty keyboard protocol, but Claude Code enables that "
"protocol only for terminals on a hardcoded list, so I send the Option+Enter "
"newline it does recognize instead. Both go away once upstream catches up."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5856
msgid ""
"The built-in =switch_session= binding only steps one session at a time.  "
"=felis-switch= (=Ctrl+Shift+p=, via the =run= action) instead pipes =felis "
"sessions list= through fzf, previewing each session's grid in colour, and "
"switches to the pick. It and its two siblings read the list as =--format "
"json=: felis promises that shape and explicitly reserves the right to move "
"the human table's columns, which is what broke them the last time the CLI "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5863
msgid ""
"felis makes only OSC 8 hyperlinks clickable, not the plain-text URLs that "
"fill real output, leaving that heuristic to an external tool as kitty does.  "
"=felis-hints= (=Ctrl+Shift+o=) is felis' side: the =pipe= action ships the "
"visible grid to [[https://git.natsukium.com/natsukium/spoor][spoor]], my own "
"hint picker, which overlays single-key labels and opens the pick. I chose "
"spoor over thumbs because it links felis' own VT parser and cell grid, so "
"its labels land on exactly the columns felis drew; thumbs rebuilds the grid "
"itself and drifts on a wide character or soft wrap. The pick opens rather "
"than landing back at the prompt: felis now exports the originating session "
"id, so typing it back is possible, but opening is what I reach for."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5873
msgid ""
"=felis-nix-log= (=Ctrl+Shift+l=, ported from kitty) scans the grid for a "
"=nix log <drv>= line and pages that build log. It uses grep + fzf rather "
"than a label overlay because a hint picker can't suppress its built-in path "
"matchers and the point here is matching *only* the =.drv=; a lone drv, the "
"usual failed-build case, opens with no picker at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: paragraph
#: modules/configuration.org:5879
msgid ""
"Desktop notifications now come from felis' own home-manager module, not a "
"helper of mine: =notifications.enable= runs a relay that streams =felis "
"notifications subscribe= and forwards each alert to =terminal-notifier= "
"(macOS) or =notify-send= (Linux), surfacing only detached sessions since an "
"attached one already flashes its own window. It replaces the subscribe loop "
"I used to hand-roll here."
msgstr ""

